            "review_title": "Review at Pizza Juventus",
            "review_text": "Erick W\nO'Fallon, Missouri86 contributions\n0\nflavorless pricey pizza with terrible dough\nNov 2024 • Solo\nFrom the outside the restaurant had some appeal. Small (8 tables, each for 4 people) but wit a rather interesting setup. Walking by I checked reviews on the web. Only a few and mainly on FB. All praising the restaurant. No customer sitting but it was early in the evening so I decided to try. Big mistake. The pizza I chose (tuna) was bland, totally flavorless. Super thin crust. No pizza dough (bread), just something white, totally flavorless supporting a touch a tomato sauce (tiny tiny touch ... I could not believe my eyes tbh), some flavorless bad mozzarella and canned tuna. The 32 cm pizza size was VND 165'000, a hefty price for what it was but above all nothing that even from far looked like an Italian pizza, not to mention the taste. Even the hot sauce with piment (not sure it was olive oil... frankly I very much doubt it) was not hot at all. I used tons of pepper and the available tabasco sauce to bring some \"flavor\" to the pizza. My strong advice: skip that restaurant if you like pizzas (pizze ;-) as theirs are truly a shame.\n\nFinal note: I got even more punished for my poor choice and lack of common sense ... suffering from diabetes type 2 I usually get spikes after eating pizze (and bread..and ... and... and ;-). This pizza triggered an all time high with 295 mg/dL (>16.5). Usually with better dough (same size) it oscillates between 9 and 12... so much for the quality and/or the ingredients.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten November 18, 2024",
